Theorem TF-11a: Terminator backward demand table

  Preconditions:
    - TF-11a emits backward demand at terminator boundaries per
      Annex E §AIMS TF-11a
    - Terminator set per ArcTerminator enumeration: Return / Jump / Branch /
      Switch / Invoke / InvokeIndirect / Resume / Unreachable (8 terminators)
    - Invoke + InvokeIndirect demands are IC-3 refined identically to
      Apply + ApplyIndirect at TF-11 (interprocedural-contract refinement
      shared between the call-instruction TF-11 path and the unwinding-
      terminator TF-11a path)
    - Resume and Unreachable are TERMINAL — neither defines a dst nor reads
      operands as USES; backward demand is empty
    - Per Annex E §AIMS TF-11a + IA-3: terminal blocks (Return / Resume /
      Unreachable) seed block exit state from TF-11a demand

  Soundness property:
    Forall terminator in ArcTerminator.
      backward_demand_tf11a(terminator) = expected per the §3 TF-11a table row
    AND L-6 monotonicity vacuous for terminator demands — each entry is a
    constant demand list (no input state to monotone over).

  Proof obligation:
    Two-part discharge:
      (a) Per-terminator demand-table enumeration — 8 terminators per the
          §3 TF-11a table.
      (b) Coverage closure — verify the 8-entry table is exhaustive over the
          ArcTerminator enumeration (no missing variant).

    Part (a) — per-terminator demand-table enumeration:
      Per Annex E §AIMS TF-11a table:
        Return { value } -> (value, Once)
        Jump { args } -> (arg, Once) per arg
        Branch { cond } -> (cond, Once)
        Switch { scrutinee } -> (scrutinee, Once)
        Invoke { args } -> (arg, Once) per arg (IC-3 refined)
        InvokeIndirect { closure, args } -> (closure, Once) + (arg, Once)/arg
        Resume -> none (terminal)
        Unreachable -> none (terminal)
      Verified: backward_demand_tf11a_lookup() enumerates every row above
      EXACTLY and produces the demand list verbatim. 8-row table closed.

    Part (b) — coverage closure:
      The ArcTerminator enumeration has cardinality 8 per Annex E §AIMS
      TF-11a. Verified: tf11a_member_set() returns the 8-element
      {Return, Jump, Branch, Switch, Invoke, InvokeIndirect, Resume,
      Unreachable} set; no additional variants exist; no Annex E §AIMS TF
      enum extension is missing.

    Engines dispatched:
      monotonicity (PRIMARY — vacuous monotonicity for constant terminator
        demand lists per section_04::verify_tf11a_terminator_demand)
      case_analysis (PRIMARY — 8-row terminator demand-table enumeration per
        section_04::verify_tf11a_terminator_demand)
      lattice (SECONDARY — accepts gracefully; no codomain state to compare)
      refinement (SECONDARY — accepts gracefully; TF-11a Invoke/InvokeIndirect
        IC-3 refinement modeled at TF-11 — TF-11a row inherits)

  Expected:
    status: valid
    reason: section_04 monotonicity + case_analysis engines discharge TF-11a via 8-row terminator demand-table enumeration + coverage closure over ArcTerminator
